cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Primes: prime-number research on the Factor Skyline"
message: "If you use this collection, please cite it."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Proxmire
    given-names: Allen
repository-code: "https://github.com/allen-proxmire/Primes"
abstract: >-
  A curated collection of prime-number research organised as five reading
  series. Several strands turn out to be one story: the primes seen through
  doubling and through the wheel (the primorials), on a coordinate system
  that gives the number line back a dimension it was hiding. Includes the
  Factor Skyline framework, the Twin-Prime Bertrand Postulate, a polyhedral
  reinterpretation of the Tao-Trudgian-Yang Exponent Database, and a
  null-model discipline with reproduction scripts for every measured table.
keywords:
  - number theory
  - prime numbers
  - prime gaps
  - twin primes
  - sieve theory
  - reproducible research
license: CC-BY-4.0
identifiers:
